      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is also well above the usual maximum single dose of about 850 to 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg total daily:** for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals, or 566 mg three times daily (not a standard tablet size).\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals:** common standard regimens.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is intentional. If it is, I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it."
      }
     ],
